+/* tools/hcr_probe/offsets.h - same origin as kmod/offsets.h (generated by gen_offsets.py).
+ * Target kernel: 5.10.97-19-9000x #20-KYLINOS SMP PREEMPT Wed Jan 21 09:21:14 UTC 2026
+ * Copied into a standalone file so this probe module does not depend on the kmod/
+ * directory and does not modify existing modules. */
+#ifndef KIF_OFFSETS_H
+#define KIF_OFFSETS_H
+
+#define KIF_UTS_RELEASE	"5.10.97-19-9000x"
+#define KIF_UTS_VERSION	"#20-KYLINOS SMP PREEMPT Wed Jan 21 09:21:14 UTC 2026"
+
+#define KIF_HCR_OFF	2200	/* vcpu->arch.hcr_el2 */
+#define KIF_ESR_OFF	2216	/* vcpu->arch.fault.esr_el2 */
+#define KIF_GPR_OFF	384	/* vcpu->arch.ctxt.gp_regs (struct kvm_cpu_context) */
+
+/* Offset of the world-switch call point (bl __kvm_vcpu_run) inside kvm_arch_vcpu_ioctl_run */
+#define KIF_RUN_CALL_OFF	1748	/* at the bl instruction: before entering the guest */
+#define KIF_RUN_POST_OFF	1752	/* bl+4: after leaving the guest */
+#define KIF_RUN_VCPU_REG	28	/* register holding vcpu at that point (x28) */
+
+#endif
--- a/kmod/hcr_probe/README.md
+++ b/kmod/hcr_probe/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+# kmod/hcr_probe - HCR_EL2.API/APK(TVM) PAC trap module
+
+Standalone kmod; does not modify `kmod/kvm_isar1_fix.c`. It is added to the
+bundle by `patches/kmod/0001-add-hcr-probe-module.patch`.
+
+## Why it is needed
+
+On this kernel (`CONFIG_ARM64_PTR_AUTH=n`) the host KVM does not virtualise the
+Apple PAC keys, so `hcr_probe` sets `HCR_EL2.API/APK/TID3` on every vCPU entry.
+Without it the guest dies on the first PAC instruction, long before the XNU
+handoff. The launcher loads it together with `kvm_cache_norm`, `kvm_psci11` and
+`kvm_isar1_fix` (`KMOD_HCR=0` skips it, `KMOD_LOAD=0` skips all four).
+
+## Polarity to remember first
+
+| Bit | Value | Effect |
+|----|----|------|
+| `HCR_EL2.API` (41) | 0 | **trap** PAC instructions to EL2 (ESR EC=0x09 -> `kvm_handle_ptrauth` -> inject UNDEF) |
+| `HCR_EL2.API` (41) | 1 | no trap, PAC executes natively |
+| `HCR_EL2.APK` (40) | 0 | **trap** `AP*Key_EL1` accesses (EC=0x18) |
+| `HCR_EL2.TVM` (26) | 1 | trap guest EL1 **writes** to SCTLR_EL1/TTBR0-1/TCR/ESR/FAR/AFSR/MAIR/AMAIR/CONTEXTIDR |
+| `HCR_EL2.TRVM` (30) | 1 | **reads** of the same set |
+
+The API trap only happens when `SCTLR_EL1.EnIA=1` (with En=0, PAC is already a
+NOP).
+
+## Build / load
+
+```bash
+# from the bundle root, after applying patches/kmod/0001-add-hcr-probe-module.patch
+make -C kmod/hcr_probe KDIR=/lib/modules/$(uname -r)/build
+
+sudo insmod kmod/hcr_probe/hcr_probe.ko hcr_api=1 hcr_apk=1 hcr_tid3=1
+```
+
+Read counters via `cat /proc/hcr_probe` or `dmesg | grep hcr_probe`.
+
+## Module parameters
+
+| Parameter | Values | Description |
+|------|------|------|
+| `hcr_api` | -1/0/1 | HCR_EL2.API: -1 leave alone, 0=**enable trap**, 1=native |
+| `hcr_apk` | -1/0/1 | HCR_EL2.APK: -1 leave alone, 0=trap key accesses, 1=allow |
+| `hcr_tid3` | 0/1 | Set TID3 (trap ID reads; needed for the ISAR1 rewrite) |
+| `hcr_tvm` | 0/1 | Set TVM (trap SCTLR_EL1 etc. writes) |
+| `clear_sctlr_en` | bool | Clear EnIA/EnIB/EnDA/EnDB in trapped SCTLR_EL1 writes |
+| `clear_at_entry` | bool | Clear context En bits before every guest entry |
+| `probe_ptrauth` / `probe_sys_reg` / `probe_vm_reg` | bool | switches for the individual hooks |
+| `dbg` | int | Print the first N detail lines per hook |
+
+The module verifies the `uname` fingerprint (same origin as `kmod/extra/offsets.h`)
+and refuses to load if it does not match.
